{"nityan haste paRavupayamane": [{"id": "nityaM haste pARAvupayamane", "headword": "नित्यं हस्ते पाणावुपयमने", "headword_slp1": "nityaM haste pARAvupayamane", "fold": "nityan haste paRavupayamane", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The word हस्ते 'in the hand', पाणौ 'in the hand' are always necessarily called गति when used with the verb कृ in the sense of 'marriage'.\n\nTerms: गति-मध्ये", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["नित्यं हस्ते पाणावुपयमने १.४.७७", "१.४.७७", "१.४.७७ नित्यं हस्ते पाणावुपयमने"], "synonyms_slp1": ["nityaM haste pARAvupayamane १.४.७७", "१.४.७७", "१.४.७७ nityaM haste pARAvupayamane"]}], "nityan kriqajivikayoH": [{"id": "nityaM krIqAjIvikayoH", "headword": "नित्यं क्रीडाजीविकयोः", "headword_slp1": "nityaM krIqAjIvikayoH", "fold": "nityan kriqajivikayoH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "A word ending with a sixth case-affix is invariably compounded with a word ending with अक , when these affixes denote a sport or livelihood; and the compound is तत्-पुरुष।\n\nTerms: समास-विभक्ति-6", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["नित्यं क्रीडाजीविकयोः २.२.१७", "२.२.१७", "२.२.१७ नित्यं क्रीडाजीविकयोः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["nityaM krIqAjIvikayoH २.२.१७", "२.२.१७", "२.२.१७ nityaM krIqAjIvikayoH"]}], "nityan kOwilye gatO": [{"id": "nityaM kOwilye gatO", "headword": "नित्यं कौटिल्ये गतौ", "headword_slp1": "nityaM kOwilye gatO", "fold": "nityan kOwilye gatO", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The affix वङ् invariably comes in the sense of 'crookedness' after a simple verb expressing motion.\n\nTerms: वङ्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["नित्यं कौटिल्ये गतौ ३.१.२३", "३.१.२३", "३.१.२३ नित्यं कौटिल्ये गतौ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["nityaM kOwilye gatO ३.१.२३", "३.१.२३", "३.१.२३ nityaM kOwilye gatO"]}], "nityan paRaH parimaRe": [{"id": "nityaM paRaH parimARe", "headword": "नित्यं पणः परिमाणे", "headword_slp1": "nityaM paRaH parimARe", "fold": "nityan paRaH parimaRe", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The affix अप् comes Invariably after the verb पण् 'to barter' when the sense is that of 'measure'.\n\nTerms: अप्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["नित्यं पणः परिमाणे ३.३.६६", "३.३.६६", "३.३.६६ नित्यं पणः परिमाणे"], "synonyms_slp1": ["nityaM paRaH parimARe ३.३.६६", "३.३.६६", "३.३.६६ nityaM paRaH parimARe"]}], "nityan NitaH": [{"id": "nityaM NitaH", "headword": "नित्यं ङितः", "headword_slp1": "nityaM NitaH", "fold": "nityan NitaH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "There is always elision of the स् of the first person of the affixes that come in the room of that ल which has an indicatory ङ्।\n\nTerms: ल", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["नित्यं ङितः ३.४.९९", "३.४.९९", "३.४.९९ नित्यं ङितः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["nityaM NitaH ३.४.९९", "३.४.९९", "३.४.९९ nityaM NitaH"]}], "nityan sanjYaCandasoH": [{"id": "nityaM saMjYACandasoH", "headword": "नित्यं संज्ञाछन्दसोः", "headword_slp1": "nityaM saMjYACandasoH", "fold": "nityan sanjYaCandasoH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The affix ङीप् necessarily comes in the छन्दस् (Vedas) and in forming Names after that बहुव्रीहि समास which ending in the syllable अन् loses its penultimate अ।\n\nTerms: विभक्ति-ङीप्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["नित्यं संज्ञाछन्दसोः ४.१.२९", "४.१.२९", "४.१.२९ नित्यं संज्ञाछन्दसोः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["nityaM saMjYACandasoH ४.१.२९", "४.१.२९", "४.१.२९ nityaM saMjYACandasoH"]}], "nityan sapatnyadisu": [{"id": "nityaM sapatnyAdizu", "headword": "नित्यं सपत्न्य्आदिषु", "headword_slp1": "nityaM sapatnyAdizu", "fold": "nityan sapatnyadisu", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "In forming the feminine with the affix ङीप् the word पति always takes the substitute न् in the words like सपत्नि etc.\n\nTerms: विभक्ति-ङीप्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["नित्यं सपत्न्य्आदिषु ४.१.३५", "४.१.३५", "४.१.३५ नित्यं सपत्न्य्आदिषु"], "synonyms_slp1": ["nityaM sapatnyAdizu ४.१.३५", "४.१.३५", "४.१.३५ nityaM sapatnyAdizu"]}], "nityan Candasi": [{"id": "nityaM Candasi", "headword": "नित्यं छन्दसि", "headword_slp1": "nityaM Candasi", "fold": "nityan Candasi", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The affix ङीष् is always used in the छन्दस् (Vedas) in forming the feminine of the words बहु etc.\n\nTerms: विभक्ति-ङीष्", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Short ऋ is invariably substituted in the छन्दस् (Vedas) for the penultimate ऋ or ॠ of a Causative अङ्ग (stem) in the reduplicated Aorist.\n\nTerms: ऋ substitute", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["नित्यं छन्दसि ४.१.४६", "नित्यं छन्दसि ७.४.८", "४.१.४६", "४.१.४६ नित्यं छन्दसि", "७.४.८", "७.४.८ नित्यं छन्दसि"], "synonyms_slp1": ["nityaM Candasi ४.१.४६", "nityaM Candasi ७.४.८", "४.१.४६", "४.१.४६ nityaM Candasi", "७.४.८", "७.४.८ nityaM Candasi"]}], "nityan vfdDasaradiByaH": [{"id": "nityaM vfdDaSarAdiByaH", "headword": "नित्यं वृद्धशरादिभ्यः", "headword_slp1": "nityaM vfdDaSarAdiByaH", "fold": "nityan vfdDasaradiByaH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The affix मयट् comes in the sense of 'product' and 'part' when neither food nor clothing is spoken of, invariably after वृद्ध words and शर etc.\n\nTerms: मयट्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["नित्यं वृद्धशरादिभ्यः ४.३.१४४", "४.३.१४४", "४.३.१४४ नित्यं वृद्धशरादिभ्यः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["nityaM vfdDaSarAdiByaH ४.३.१४४", "४.३.१४४", "४.३.१४४ nityaM vfdDaSarAdiByaH"]}], "nityan satadimasarDamasasanvatsaraca": [{"id": "nityaM SatAdimAsArDamAsasaMvatsarAcca", "headword": "नित्यं शतादिमासार्धमाससंवत्सराच्च", "headword_slp1": "nityaM SatAdimAsArDamAsasaMvatsarAcca", "fold": "nityan satadimasarDamasasanvatsaraca", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "After 