d directly through the agent of the causative.\n\nTerms: धातु-भी", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["नित्यं स्मयतेः ६.१.५७", "६.१.५७", "६.१.५७ नित्यं स्मयतेः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["nityaM smayateH ६.१.५७", "६.१.५७", "६.१.५७ nityaM smayateH"]}], "nityamamreqite qaci": [{"id": "nityamAmreqite qAci", "headword": "नित्यमाम्रेडिते डाचि", "headword_slp1": "nityamAmreqite qAci", "fold": "nityamamreqite qaci", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "Of such a doubled sound-imitation word, to which the affix आ is added which causes elision of the final अत् , for the final त् of the first member and the initial consonant of the second member, such subsequent consonant is always the single substitute.\n\nTerms: संहितायाम्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["नित्यमाम्रेडिते डाचि ६.१.१००", "६.१.१००", "६.१.१०० नित्यमाम्रेडिते डाचि"], "synonyms_slp1": ["nityamAmreqite qAci ६.१.१००", "६.१.१००", "६.१.१०० nityamAmreqite qAci"]}], "nityan mantre": [{"id": "nityaM mantre", "headword": "नित्यं मन्त्रे", "headword_slp1": "nityaM mantre", "fold": "nityan mantre", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "In the मन्त्राः , these words जुष्ट and अर्पित have always the acute on the first syllable.\n\nTerms: accent-छन्दस", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["नित्यं मन्त्रे ६.१.२१०", "६.१.२१०", "६.१.२१० नित्यं मन्त्रे"], "synonyms_slp1": ["nityaM mantre ६.१.२१०", "६.१.२१०", "६.१.२१० nityaM mantre"]}], "nityan karoteH": [{"id": "nityaM karoteH", "headword": "नित्यं करोतेः", "headword_slp1": "nityaM karoteH", "fold": "nityan karoteH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The elision of उ is invariable before व् and म् in the case of कृ 'to make' (करोति).\n\nTerms: कित् and ङित्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["नित्यं करोतेः ६.४.१०८", "६.४.१०८", "६.४.१०८ नित्यं करोतेः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["nityaM karoteH ६.४.१०८", "६.४.१०८", "६.४.१०८ nityaM karoteH